{"type": "message", "id": "5eef1ba2", "parentId": "005fa2c9", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T03:15:08.470Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_a4e1704a20f14f43be0e72bd", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"most deadly cancers United States 5-year survival rate statistics 2024\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 9751,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0061c87dd1be53d5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2024 - Siegel - 2024 - CA: A Cancer Journal for Clinicians - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0061c87dd1be53d5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://acsjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.3322/caac.21820\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e72b8873d2723bee\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe 5-year relative survival rate for all cancers combined improved from 58% during the mid-1970s to 85% during 2013 through 2019 in children and from 68% to 87% in adolescents but varies substantially by cancer type and age at diagnosis (Table 14). The estimated numbers of new cancer cases and deaths in 2024 provide a reasonably accurate portrayal of the contemporary cancer burden.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e72b8873d2723bee\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 17, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"acsjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1aafd6aa5c9a6561\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1aafd6aa5c9a6561\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statis