680\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMultiple myeloma: 2024 update on diagnosis, risk‐stratification, and management\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bb27f1061eef5680\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ajh.27422\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f8ecd26233c94f8d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMultiple myeloma accounts for 1% of all cancers and approximately 10% of all hematologic malignancies.1 Each year <strong>over 35 000</strong> new cases are diagnosed in the United States, and almost 13 000 patients die of the disease.2 The annual age-adjusted ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f8ecd26233c94f8d\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 28, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5aca9225620a6802\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMultiple myeloma incidence and mortality trends in the United States, 1999–2020 | Scientific Reports\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5aca9225620a6802\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-65590-4\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"48b4f1844ec482e7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMultiple myeloma (MM) is a plasma cell disorder accounting for approximately 10% of hematologic malignancies. There is limited epidemiological evidence regarding the long-term trends and disparities in MM in the US. We conducted a multiple time point cross-sectional study using MM incidence ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"48b4f1844ec482e7\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 24, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nature.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"add2b5e3ff3eedb6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA population-based study on incidence trends of myeloma in the United States over 2000–2020 | Scientific Reports\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"add2b5e3ff3eedb6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-47906-y\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"06a2718aae757a66\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMyeloma is one of the most common types of haematological malignancies. We aimed to investigate the incidence rates of myeloma by sex, race, age, and histological subgroups in the United States (US) over 2000–2020. Data were retrieved from the the Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"06a2718aae757a66\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"November 24, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nature.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0340fd066d2818de\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhat are the most recent myeloma statistics? - HealthTree for Multiple Myeloma\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0340fd066d2818de\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://healthtree.org/myeloma/community/articles/annual-survival-rate-statistics-update-multiple-myeloma-rate-unchanged\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"89d670c7e6de3495\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>In 2023, the estimated new myeloma cases were 35,730, accounting for 1.8% of all new cancer cases</strong>, whereas the estimated deaths in 2023 only accounted for 12,590, representing 2.1% of all cancer deaths.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"89d670c7e6de3495\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 9, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"healthtree.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9e4d6364ab05c7c1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMultiple Myeloma: Data Reports 2026\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9e4d6364ab05c7c1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://wifitalents.com/multiple-myeloma-statistics/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"61cb80947b58c906\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe lifetime risk of getting multiple myeloma is about 1 in 103 (0.97%) In 2024, <strong>an estimated 35,780 new cases will be diagnosed in the United States</strong>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"61cb80947b58c906\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 12, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"wifitalents.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b2581db3b6c6dd7f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMultiple Myeloma: 2022 update on Diagnosis, Risk-stratification and Management - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b2581db3b6c6dd7f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9387011/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43895661b3022a75\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMultiple myeloma accounts for 1% of all cancers and approximately 10% of all hematologic malignancies.1,2 Each year <strong>over 32,000</strong> new cases are diagnosed in the United States, and almost 13,000 patients die of the disease.3 The annual age-adjusted incidence in the United States has remained stable ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43895661b3022a75\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43140611ef82bd83\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWho Gets Multiple Myeloma?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43140611ef82bd83\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.webmd.com/cancer/multiple-myeloma/who-gets-multiple-myeloma\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e3703375c856fc01\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the U.S., they’re up 143% since 1975. <strong>An estimated 35,780 Americans were expected to be diagnosed with multiple myeloma in 2024</strong>. In the U.S., multiple myeloma accounts for almost 2% of new cancer cases and more than 2% of cancer deaths.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\